                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9dbd303e-37ba-3c56-a64f-02f0d04bfbce",
                                        "entry_id": "f0a6cd93-f051-3bcb-b136-ffc0c63ad49e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Able but not certain to happen; neither inevitable nor impossible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0968937b-5322-443d-b608-a1560aa8bc77",
                                                "sense_id": "9dbd303e-37ba-3c56-a64f-02f0d04bfbce",
                                                "text": "Rain tomorrow is possible, but I wouldn't bet on it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b03fdb16-ca75-4e52-9853-c68976009adf",
                                                "sense_id": "9dbd303e-37ba-3c56-a64f-02f0d04bfbce",
                                                "text": "It's not just possible, it's probable that there will be rain tomorrow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7e5ad12-4fbc-4bc4-b905-b31f37470e1e",
                                                "sense_id": "9dbd303e-37ba-3c56-a64f-02f0d04bfbce",
                                                "text": "The humor of my proposition appealed more strongly to Miss Trevor than I had looked for, and from that time forward she became her old self again;[…]. Now she had come to look upon the matter in its true proportions, and her anticipation of a possible chance of teaching him a lesson was a pleasure to behold."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "168b6a4a-b731-3728-888d-672a7a0f71c6",
                                        "entry_id": "f0a6cd93-f051-3bcb-b136-ffc0c63ad49e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Capable of being done or achieved; feasible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c711500d-3710-40b7-9997-53a5f2ee4681",
                                                "sense_id": "168b6a4a-b731-3728-888d-672a7a0f71c6",
                                                "text": "It's possible for anyone to learn to play the bagpipes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd822be7-2d48-42a4-bef6-f80e6360e2d4",
                                                "sense_id": "168b6a4a-b731-3728-888d-672a7a0f71c6",
                                                "text": "And success in minor degree, in the sense in which he uses the term \"success,\" is only somewhat more possible than success in winning the White House chair."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ff72ffe-693c-422d-aa5a-ba9296dbbe65",
                                                "sense_id": "168b6a4a-b731-3728-888d-672a7a0f71c6",
                                                "text": "Peace between Israel and the Arab countries is \"more possible than any time before,\" says ex-Arab League U.N. ambassador Clovis Maskoud."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0101d380-8311-4fe1-80e4-eb320f8cf2f8",
                                                "sense_id": "168b6a4a-b731-3728-888d-672a7a0f71c6",
                                                "text": "Mostly, the microbiome is beneficial. It helps with digestion and enables people to extract a lot more calories from their food than would otherwise be possible. Research over the past few years, however, has implicated it in diseases from atherosclerosis to asthma to autism."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "889d916a-7fe8-343a-a303-4c260c6803c2",
                                        "entry_id": "f0a6cd93-f051-3bcb-b136-ffc0c63ad49e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Being considered, e.g. for a position."
